      body: "Think of an EC2 instance as a hotel room. The **ENI** is the room's phone line with its own number; the hotel can unplug that line and plug it into another room, so callers keep dialing the same number. **ENA** is upgrading that line to fiber, and **EFA** is a private intercom between rooms that skips the switchboard entirely.\n\nThe **metadata service** is the front desk you can call from inside the room: 'What room am I in? What is my key code?' IMDSv2 makes the desk ask for a one-time password first, so a stranger who tricks you into relaying a call cannot get your key. **Stopping** is checking out but keeping your luggage in storage (EBS); **hibernating** is freezing time with your work still laid out on the desk; **terminating** is checking out and throwing everything away. A **golden AMI** is a pre-furnished room template, so new rooms are ready instantly instead of being furnished after guests arrive.",
